# erbq-event.te — the strong point-event#1 form (count panel over the driver-quantile bins).
# witness: point-event#1 (Tohoku seismicity, phi/witnesses.φ); driver: solar-wind IMF Bz, 60 s.
# form event-conditional refuses at parse if either arm is absent; `count quantile 8` runs the
# count panel (q = largest power of two with n/q >= 20 for n = 198 -> 8, expected ~24.75/bin).
# The panel tests observed bin counts against the exposure-weighted expectation; the verdict is the
# empirical rank p (1 + #{>=obs})/(B+1) with a Benjamini-Hochberg step over the bins (Phipson & Smyth
# 2010; Theiler 1992). mean+2sd stays screening only. B = 1000 resolves q/alpha = 160 at alpha 0.05.
# The event times stay fixed; only the driver shifts, so the Omori clustering is part of the null.
# The declustered mainshock set is a named side deliverable (An mountain), not a prerequisite.
pair erbq-event
form event-conditional
witness point-event#1
driver omni_hro_imf_bz_gsm_nt
count quantile 8
cadence live
bin 3600
surrogate 1000
